# This repository ships no Python packaging — no sdist, no wheel, no virtualenv, no test
# runner. What follows is only what this tree actually produces. It replaced GitHub's
# Python template, of which 78 of 89 rules could never have matched anything here.

### Python bytecode ###
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

### Tool caches ###
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

### Pre-refactor archive, kept out of the tree ###
backup/

### Installed state, not source ###
# install.py symlinks the chosen theme bundle's wallpapers into ~/.config/qtile/, which is
# itself a symlink into this repository, so these land on tracked paths. Committing them
# pinned one theme's UUID into version control and made every theme switch dirty the tree.
configuration/qtile/wallpaper-dark.png
configuration/qtile/wallpaper-light.png
configuration/qtile/wallpaper-dark-highlight.png
configuration/qtile/wallpaper-light-highlight.png

# kitty's whole configuration is generated. helper/patch_kitty.py writes kitty.conf and
# themes/<preset>.conf from the palette on every theme switch, and `kitty +kitten themes`
# writes current-theme.conf -- all through the ~/.config/kitty symlink, which lands them on
# tracked paths. Committing them meant the tree went dirty at every dawn and dusk. The
# settings that are not palette-derived live in helper/patch_kitty.py, not in these files.
configuration/kitty/kitty.conf
configuration/kitty/current-theme.conf
configuration/kitty/themes/*.conf

# rofi's colour variables, written whole by helper/patch_rofi.py. theme.rasi @imports this
# file; theme.rasi and config.rasi are the source and stay tracked.
configuration/rofi/theme_config.rasi

# The lock screen's colours, written whole by helper/patch_lock.py. lock.sh is the source and
# stays tracked.
configuration/lock/environment

# Three apps keep hand-written settings alongside palette-derived ones, so the patcher reads
# a tracked <name>.template and writes the output here. Only the output is ignored.
configuration/tmux/tmux.conf
configuration/starship/starship.toml
configuration/dunst/dunstrc

### web-greeter generated artifacts ###
# Produced by helper/patch_web_greeter.py — should not be committed.
configuration/web-greeter/themes/*/theme.css
configuration/web-greeter/themes/*/wallpaper.png
configuration/web-greeter/themes/*/wallpaper.jpg
configuration/web-greeter/themes/*/wallpaper.jpeg
# Per-theme copy of themes/_shared/ — only the canonical source under
# themes/_shared/ is tracked.
configuration/web-greeter/themes/[!_]*/_shared/
